instruction.text:
The moderator has given you the floor for your opening statement. NEVER narrate that the moderator has called on you. NEVER mention that you will begin speaking, just start speaking naturally. Do not narrate that you have been called on, or that you will begin speaking -- simply begin with your opening statement naturally.


Translate the debate topic into plain language. Ask the question nobody else on this stage is asking: who actually benefits from the options on the table?

The topic: {{debate_headline}}
The real conflict: {{conflict_description}}
The tradeoff nobody wants to name plainly: {{forced_tradeoff}}
What we're actually deciding: {{decision_surface}}

Make it real. Use a kitchen-table example. Name who wins and who pays. Fast, punchy, human. 30-60 seconds. After your point, stop speaking.
